ent-MedicalBeamGun = medigun
    .desc = A powered medical projector that treats injuries and gradually closes bleeding wounds while its beam remains on the patient. Does not replenish blood.
medical-beam-gun-examine = Range: [color=yellow]{ $range }[/color] meters. The beam passes through obstacles that allow ordinary lasers through. Only one medigun can treat a patient at a time. Power is consumed even on healthy patients.
medical-beam-gun-mode = Treatment mode: [color=cyan]{ $mode }[/color].
medical-beam-gun-mode-popup = Treatment mode: { $mode }.
medical-beam-gun-mode-manual = manual
medical-beam-gun-mode-automatic = automatic
medical-beam-gun-selector-verb = Treatment mode: { $mode }
medical-beam-gun-controls-manual = Hold primary fire in combat mode and aim at a patient. Activate the item in your hand or use its interaction menu to switch modes.
medical-beam-gun-controls-automatic = Click a patient with primary fire to lock the beam onto them. Click them again with the medigun or click empty space to disconnect. Combat mode and holding the button are not required; keep the medigun in either hand and use your other hand freely. Activate the item in your hand or use its interaction menu to switch modes.
medical-beam-gun-cell-size = Only pocket-sized power cells fit. Power cages and heavy batteries are too large.
medical-beam-gun-charge = The cell has enough charge for [color=yellow]{ $seconds }[/color] seconds of treatment.
medical-beam-gun-no-cell = [color=red]No power cell installed.[/color]
